<section class="hero"><div class="top"><div class="admin-brand-head"><div id="adminCube" class="admin-cube"></div><div><div class="eyebrow">LOOM v<span id="adminCanonicalVersion">0.15.18</span> · ADMINISTRATOR CONSOLE</div><h1>LOOM Admin</h1><p>Global LOOM configuration, project settings, user administration, moderation, and persistence.</p></div></div><div class="nav"><a id="appLink" href="../projects/green-beans/app/?project=green-beans">Open selected project</a></div></div><div class="identity"><span class="pill" id="who">Loading identity…</span><span class="pill">Privilege: Admin</span><span class="pill warn" id="storagePill">Checking storage…</span></div><div class="danger-note">User changes are auditable and require typing <b>CONFIRM</b>. IP addresses are captured as network metadata only; LOOM never uses IP as authentication proof or as the identity used for bans.</div></section>
<div class="toolbar"><div id="projectChooser" class="hidden"><strong>Project</strong> <select id="project"></select></div><div class="tabs"><button class="tab active" data-tab="loom">LOOM Settings</button><button class="tab" data-tab="project">Project Settings</button><button class="tab" data-tab="users">Users</button><button class="tab" data-tab="identities">Identity Manager</button><button class="tab" data-tab="access">Access</button><button class="tab" data-tab="database">Database</button></div></div>
<section id="loomSettingsPanel" class="panel active"><div class="eyebrow">GLOBAL LOOM CORE SETTINGS</div><h2>LOOM Settings</h2><p>These settings belong to the LOOM engine itself and apply across LOOM-owned surfaces and all projects where relevant.</p><main id="globalModules" class="grid" style="margin-top:14px"></main></section>
<section id="projectSettingsPanel" class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SELECTED PROJECT SETTINGS</div><h2>Project Settings</h2><p>Project identity is managed here; module configuration stays modular below it.</p><section id="projectPresentationCard" class="module" style="margin-top:14px" data-admin-static-section="project-presentation" data-admin-title="Module Presentation"></section><section class="module-control" data-admin-static-section="module-control" data-admin-title="Module Control Center"><div class="module-control-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">MODULE CONTROL CENTER</div><h2 style="margin:4px 0 3px">Every LOOM + project module</h2><p style="margin:0">Enable modules, control responsive loading, and optionally override each module’s title-bar/collapse behavior.</p></div><input id="moduleControlSearch" class="module-control-search" placeholder="Search modules, IDs, source…"></div><div id="moduleControlList" class="module-control-list"></div></section><section id="projectProfileCard" class="module" style="margin-top:14px" data-admin-static-section="project-profile" data-admin-title="Project Identity"></section><div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:22px">PROJECT MODULE SETTINGS</div><main id="modules" class="grid" style="margin-top:10px"></main></section>
<section id="usersPanel" class="panel"><div class="users-layout"><div><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT USERS</div><h2>User control</h2><p>Bans are project-specific and never delete the account.</p><div class="user-search"><input id="userSearch" placeholder="Search username, email, ID, IP"><button id="userRefresh" class="secondary">↻</button></div><div id="userList" class="user-list"></div></div><div id="userDetail" class="user-detail"><div class="empty">Select a user or client profile.</div></div></div></section>
<section id="identitiesPanel" class="panel"><div class="users-layout"><div><div class="eyebrow">DURABLE GUEST IDENTITIES</div><h2>Identity Manager</h2><p>Guest data is permanent by default. Search, investigate, issue recovery codes, or attach preserved Guest History to a permanent account.</p><div class="user-search"><input id="identitySearch" placeholder="Search guest ID, client, user ID"><button id="identityRefresh" class="secondary">↻</button></div><div id="identityList" class="user-list"></div></div><div id="identityDetail" class="user-detail"><div class="empty">Select a Guest Identity.</div></div></div></section>
<section id="accessPanel" class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">DELEGATED ADMINISTRATION</div><h2>Access Manager</h2><p>The System Owner is the immutable root authority. Delegate LOOM-wide Admin access to permanent accounts, or project-only Admin/Manager access to permanent accounts and Guest Identities.</p><div id="accessSummary" class="status-row" style="margin-top:12px"></div><div class="grid" style="margin-top:14px"><section id="loomAdminAccessCard" class="module"><div class="eyebrow">LOOM-WIDE</div><h2>LOOM Admins</h2><p>Only the System Owner can add or revoke secondary LOOM Admins. They remain one tier below System Owner.</p><div class="field"><label>Permanent account</label><select id="loomAdminSubject"></select></div><div class="buttons"><button id="grantLoomAdmin" class="save">Grant LOOM Admin</button></div><div id="loomAdminList" class="setup"></div></section><section class="module"><div class="eyebrow">PROJECT-SCOPED</div><h2>Project Admin / Manager</h2><p>Project access never grants unrelated-project or LOOM-global authority.</p><div class="field"><label>Account / Guest Identity</label><select id="projectAccessSubject"></select></div><div class="field"><label>Role</label><select id="projectAccessRole"><option value="project-manager">Project Manager</option><option value="project-admin">Project Admin</option></select></div><div class="buttons"><button id="grantProjectAccess" class="save">Grant Project Access</button></div><div id="projectAccessList" class="setup"></div></section></div><div id="accessMsg" class="msg"></div></section>
<section id="databasePanel" class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SQL PERSISTENCE</div><h2>MySQL / MariaDB</h2><p>Temporary files remain available before SQL connection. Once initialized/migrated, SQL is the durable persistence layer.</p><div id="dbStatus" class="status-row"></div><div class="db-grid"><div class="field"><label>Database host</label><input id="dbHost" type="text"></div><div class="field"><label>Port</label><input id="dbPort" type="number" value="3306"></div><div class="field"><label>Database name</label><input id="dbName" type="text"></div><div class="field"><label>Database username</label><input id="dbUser" type="text"></div><div class="field"><label>Password</label><input id="dbPass" type="password" placeholder="Leave blank to keep saved password"></div></div><div class="buttons"><button id="dbSave" class="save">1. Save & Test Connection</button><button id="dbInit" class="secondary">2. Initialize / Update Tables</button><button id="dbMigrate" class="secondary">3. Migrate Temporary Data</button></div><div id="dbMsg" class="msg"></div><div class="setup"><b>Existing database?</b> Running Initialize / Update Tables again is safe; LOOM schema updates use non-destructive <code>CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS</code> statements where applicable.</div><div class="module" style="margin-top:16px"><div class="eyebrow">DATABASE INTEGRITY DOCTOR</div><h2>Audit before you repair</h2><p>Scans LOOM identity/account relationships without changing data. Safe Repair always creates a protected full LOOM-table snapshot first. It restores/validates the parent permanent-user row before repairing username, authentication, client, and Admin child mappings, then cleans expired login sessions. It never deletes user accounts, project history, events, avatars, or moderation records.</p><div class="buttons"><button id="integrityScan" class="secondary">Scan Integrity</button><button id="integrityBackup" class="reset">Create Snapshot</button><button id="integrityRepair" class="danger">Safe Repair…</button></div><div id="integritySummary" class="status-row" style="margin-top:12px"></div><div id="integrityIssues" class="setup">Run a scan to inspect the database.</div><div id="integrityMsg" class="msg"></div></div></section>
</div><script src="../engine/identity.js?v=0.15.19"></script><script src="../engine/loom-brand.js?v=0.15.19"></script><script>
